## Head-to-head: the three closest pairs

### Webapp Testing vs Playwright Skill: which browser-testing skill to pick

Both drive a real browser and both are about local web apps. The difference is language and lifecycle.

| | Webapp Testing | Playwright Skill |
| :-- | :-- | :-- |
| Language | Python Playwright | Node Playwright |
| Server handling | `with_server.py` starts and stops servers, multi-server aware | Detects already-running dev servers, asks which URL if several |
| Setup | No install step in the SKILL.md | `npm run setup` once (installs Playwright and Chromium) |
| Browser mode | Headless chromium | Visible by default, headless on request |
| Catalog installs (Nov 26, 2026) | 353 | 29 |
| Folder last commit | April 20, 2026 | August 14, 2026 |
| License (GitHub API) | none reported, LICENSE.txt in folder | MIT |

**Pick Webapp Testing** if your project is Python-leaning or you need the agent to start the backend and frontend together. **Pick Playwright Skill** if your repo is JavaScript and you want scripts saved next to your code. Do not install both; they will compete for the same "test my web app" prompts.

### Frontend Design vs UI UX Pro Max: which design skill to pick

| | Frontend Design | UI UX Pro Max |
| :-- | :-- | :-- |
| Approach | A process: plan, review against the brief, build, critique | A database you query with a script |
| Idle context cost | About 9,000 characters when loaded | Larger SKILL.md plus data, scripts and references upstream |
| Catalog installs | 481 | 1,909 |
| Codex readiness | Plain SKILL.md, nothing path-specific | Catalog copy uses `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` paths; the repo documents `uipro init --ai codex` |
| Last folder commit | September 3, 2026 | November 26, 2026 |

**Pick Frontend Design** to get distinctive, deliberate visual choices on a single page with no setup. **Pick UI UX Pro Max** when you want a repeatable, queryable design system and are willing to run its installer. If you only install one for Codex today, Frontend Design is the lower-risk choice because nothing in it assumes another agent's directory layout.

### Skill Installer vs the catalog's hosted zip: which install route to pick

| | Skill Installer (GitHub) | agentskills.codes hosted zip |
| :-- | :-- | :-- |
| What you get | The whole skill folder, scripts and references included | `SKILL.md` only (every zip we opened held one file) |
| Default destination | `$CODEX_HOME/skills`, or pass `--dest` | You choose with `unzip -d` |
| Needs | Python and network access to GitHub | `curl` and `unzip` |
| Best for | Skills with scripts: Webapp Testing, GH Fix CI, Security Best Practices | Single-file skills: Frontend Design, Turborepo, Code Reviewer |

Use the catalog to discover and read a skill, and the GitHub installer when the upstream folder has more than a SKILL.md.

{% figure src="https://opengraph.githubassets.com/1/anthropics/skills" alt="GitHub social card for the anthropics/skills repository" caption="anthropics/skills, upstream of Webapp Testing and Frontend Design. Source: GitHub" /%}

